# Business services inherit GenericService

Any specialized service in `CoperativeTelouet.Business` that manages an entity must **inherit** `GenericService<TEntity, TDto, TCreateDto, TUpdateDto>` and reuse its CRUD/validation/mapping before adding domain methods.

## Rules

- **Do** inherit `GenericService<…>` for the primary entity the service owns.
- **Do** add **custom methods** on the domain interface (`CreateClientAsync`, `GetClientsAsync`, …) that call the inherited `CreateAsync` / `UpdateAsync` / `GetByIdAsync` / `GetAllAsync`.
- **Do** keep domain interfaces standalone (e.g. `IClientService`) — do **not** extend `IGenericService` on specialized APIs so callers cannot bypass domain rules via generic CRUD.
- **Do** use **AutoMapper** for DTO ↔ entity (and DTO ↔ DTO) mapping — declare maps in `Mapping/*Profile.cs` and call `Mapper.Map<T>(…)` instead of hand-copying properties.
- **Do** use record `with { … }` after `Mapper.Map` when only one/few fields change (e.g. toggle `Actif`).
- **Do** use `Repo.FindAsync` / `FindAsync` (predicate) for filtered reads so SQL applies `WHERE` — never `GetAllAsync` then `.Where` in memory for large tables.
- **Don't** mark any `GenericService` method or member as `virtual` / `abstract` / `override` — never override the base. That is risky and destabilizes the business layer contract.
- **Don't** manually construct a DTO/entity by listing every property when an AutoMapper profile can do it.
- **Don't** duplicate validator resolution, AutoMapper mapping, or repository Add/Update/Delete in the subclass.
- **Don't** invent a parallel CRUD API that ignores `GenericService`.
- Simple catalog entities with no extra logic stay as closed `GenericService<…>` registrations in DI (no subclass needed).

## Custom method pattern (required)

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — custom method calls GenericService (no override)
public async Task<TiersDto> CreateClientAsync(CreateTiersDto dto, CancellationToken ct = default)
{
    EnsureClientType(dto.Type);
    return await CreateAsync(dto, ct);
}

// ❌ BAD — override / virtual GenericService
public override async Task<TiersDto> CreateAsync(...) { ... }
```

## AutoMapper example

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — map then tweak
var update = Mapper.Map<UpdateTiersDto>(dto) with { Actif = !dto.Actif };
await UpdateClientAsync(id, update, ct);

// ❌ BAD — hand-copy every field
await UpdateClientAsync(id, new UpdateTiersDto(dto.Type, dto.Nom, …, !dto.Actif), ct);
```

**Rule of thumb:** inherit GenericService, never virtualize/override it, expose custom domain methods that call its CRUD, AutoMapper for all mapping.
